## Boundaries

- C4Stack is a pinned dependency. Never copy its code, SQL or assets into this app;
  upgrade with `task framework:update VERSION=…`.
- The app owns `main.go`, `config.go`, `routes.go`, the layout, pages, styles and
  `migrations/`.
- Environment variables use the `[[.EnvPrefix]]_` prefix and are read in `config.go`,
  except `[[.EnvPrefix]]_DATABASE_URL`, which `main.go` passes to `app.Main` for migrate.

## C4Stack

The C4Stack guide has recipes for pages, app tables, API endpoints, credit holds,
design, providers and upgrades. Read the docs of the release in `go.mod`; when this
app was generated, they were:

- Guide: [[.Docs]]/guide.md
- Operations and runbooks: [[.Docs]]/operations.md

## Rules

- Signed-in browser routes go in the `/account` group in `routes.go`, which uses
  `accts.RequireSignIn`; public forms use `web.CSRF`. Never protect an API-key route
  with either. C4Stack's own account pages are under `/account/settings` and
  `/account/delete`.
- Read the signed-in account with `accounts.Current(c)`.
- Render pages with `layout.Render`; forms include `@ui.CSRFField(c)`.
- New tables with personal data reference `accounts (id) ON DELETE CASCADE`, or are
  cleaned in an `accts.OnDelete` hook.
- Never change a migration file once it has been applied anywhere. Add a new file.
- Enable a module (`apikeys`, `credits`, `credits/expiry`) by adding its `Migrations` to
  the list in `main.go` before the app's own, constructing it in `setup` and mounting
  its page on a group of the `/account` group, such as `/account/api-keys`.
- Prices are set on the server. Take credit with `Debit` and a reference that makes a
  retry safe. For long work, reserve credit in an app table under `WithAccount`, report
  it through the `Holds` function, and charge it with `Capture` when the work is done.
- Pass `c.Request.Context()` to database calls, never the `*gin.Context`.
- To change a shared task, list it under `excludes` in `Taskfile.yml` and define your own.
- Run `task templ:generate` after editing `.templ` files and commit the generated code.
- Never log secrets, session cookies, API keys or request bodies.
- Before finishing, run `task check` and `task test:integration`.
